ing of the "new song that I haven't finished yet" (新歌). The speaker states this happens "At the end of the performance" (在演出的尾聲).\n\nLet's estimate the timing based on the provided transcript:\n*   0:00 - ~0:05: Introduction, mentioning watching I Hate Models and 9 Times 9.\n*   ~0:05 - ~0:08: Speaker goes on stage, performs, and goes home (narrative).\n*   ~0:08 - End: Speaker mentions sharing the unfinished song ("在演出的尾聲...").\n\nThe 6-second mark divides the audio roughly in half. The mention of sharing the unfinished song occurs clearly *after* the 6-second mark, in the latter part of the clip.\n\n*   If the non-live segment is the sharing of the unfinished song, it occurs in the second half.\n\n**Step 4: Final Conclusion.**\n1. Is all music live? No.\n2. Is the non-live segment in the first half or the second half? It occurs at the end of the performance, which is in the second half of the audio clip.\n\nThis matches option C: "no; second half".\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
