2025-12-24 16:12:31 | INFO | Q675 id=BV1BPRnYAEx6_00-14-34_00-14-40 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The audio states that one steak costs "more than 50 US dollars, about 400 RMB" (牛排就要50多美元, 大概400人民幣).\nIt then states that if each person has one steak, the total cost will be "1600" (我們如果一人一份牛排就要花掉1600).\n\nLet $P$ be the price of one steak in RMB, and $N$ be the number of people.\nFrom the audio, $P \approx 400$ RMB.\nThe total cost is $N \times P = 1600$ RMB.\nTherefore, $N = \frac{1600}{P}$.\nUsing the approximate price $P=400$:\n$N = \frac{1600}{400} = 4$.\n\nThe total number of people is 4.\n\nComparing this result with the choices:\nA) 5\nB) 3\nC) 4\nD) 6\n\nThe calculated number of people is 4, which corresponds to choice C.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
