preted as being stingy or unwilling to pour it out. Given the limited context, the most direct interpretation of his negative reaction to the pouring is a disagreement with the action, which could stem from a desire not to waste the drink, perhaps by not pouring it.\n\nThe initial reasoning led to D. The second man's comment is a direct criticism of the act of pouring/wasting the drink. If he believes it's a waste, he is unlikely to want to pour his own, fitting the idea of being stingy or unwilling to pour it out.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{D}
